{"edits": [{"finding_ids": [], "search": "    input_file3: str = Field(
        ..., description="Path to input H5 file", cli=("-f", "--hdf5")
    )", "replace": "    input_file3: str = Field(
        ...,
        description="Path to input H5 file",
        json_schema_extra={"cli": ("-f", "--hdf5")},
    )", "explanation": "The failure reports Field() receiving the extra keyword 'cli', which PydanticDeprecatedSince20 flags. Per the Pydantic V2 migration guide, extra kwargs on Field are deprecated and should be passed via json_schema_extra. The value is unchanged, now nested under the 'cli' key of json_schema_extra."}, {"finding_ids": [], "search": "        cli=("-b", "--beta-filter"),", "replace": "        json_schema_extra={"cli": ("-b", "--beta-filter")},", "explanation": "Same deprecated Field extra-kwarg pattern as input_file3 (Field(cli=...) is deprecated in V2 in favor of json_schema_extra). Preserves the same cli tuple value."}, {"finding_ids": [], "search": "        cli=("--epsilon", "--disable-epsilon"),", "replace": "        json_schema_extra={"cli": ("--epsilon", "--disable-epsilon")},", "explanation": "Same deprecated Field extra-kwarg pattern (cli=...) in epsilon; moved to json_schema_extra per the V2 migration guide. Value preserved."}], "notes": "Findings handled by the current content already: (1) config-class (line 20): the class Config is gone and `model_config = ConfigDict(...)` is already present, so no edit. (2) optional-no-default for outfile (line 38) and gamma (line 55): both already read `= None`, so no edit. The collection failure came from Field(cli=...) extra kwargs, which I fixed in input_file3, beta_filter, and epsilon, since the same deprecated pattern appears in all three and would fail the same way after the first one is fixed. Cross-file dependency to check: the pydantic_cli core (core.py, not in this edit) must read the CLI flags from field_info.json_schema_extra["cli"] instead of field_info.extra["cli"], otherwise the flags will silently stop being applied. No other edits made; the rest of the file is already V2-compatible (ConfigDict, Optional fields with defaults, Field(...) for required values)."}
